what kind of monster would fire kermit  the frog why was one star kicked off her  own show and how did toby mcguire's  salary demands nearly end the spider-man  series keep watching to find out  steve whitmire the voice of kermit the  frog for 27 years was fired by disney in  2017 and there are at least three  different versions of why he was let go  speaking to the hollywood reporter  whitmire painted himself as the last  holdout from before disney's acquisition  of the muppets in 2004. he told thr he  was given two reasons for his firing for  being outspoken and critical about  changes to kermit and for refusing to  work on a specific project disney and  the muppet studio had a different story  they told the hollywood reporter  wittmeyer was quote overly hostile and  unproductive and claimed he had been  dismissed for patterns of behavior that  he'd displayed quote over the course of  many years  but according to gizmodo the real reason  was simple money unnamed sources told  gizmodo that whitmire had asked for a  higher salary than any other muppet's  performer first class flights to and  from his home and a separate salary for  his wife who worked as whitmire's  manager what they really wanted was for  me to frame this as i moved on  and that i had retired and i it was just  disingenuous instead they fired him and  the blame game began  following his appearance as the red  skull in 2011's captain america the  first avenger actor hugo weaving made it  clear that he didn't really want to  return to the mcu telling collider he  had quote done his dash with that sort  of film  of course he had already signed a  multi-picture deal but he seemed  confident that marvel wouldn't force him  to fulfill those obligations it turns  out he was right but it was mostly a  matter of money in 2020 weaving told  timeout marvel that he had actually been  willing to play the red skull again in  2018's avengers infinity war and 2019's  avengers end game but marvel had offered  him quote much less money than before  when the two sides couldn't reach an  agreement weaving was replaced by ross  marquan who couldn't have been more  thrilled i'm a huge marvel geek myself i  used to draw comic books when i was a  kid this is just this is all just very  amazing  the late valerie harper was a successful  sitcom star throughout the 70s she rose  to fame on the mary tyler marsha  eventually earning her own spin-off  series rhoda she let her own series  again in the 80s nbc's valerie in which  she played a mother trying to raise  three sons mostly on her own  coincidentally the series also proved an  early high point in the career of a  young jason bateman who played valerie's  eldest son david valerie proved a hit  and at the end of season two harper  decided to take advantage of the  situation figuring they couldn't make  her show without you know her according  to people she originally received fifty  six thousand seven hundred fifty dollars  per episode along with ten percent of  the show's adjusted gross profits for  season three harper asked for a  significant bump to one hundred thousand  dollars per episode and 35 of the  adjusted gross profits when nbc said no  harper stopped showing up for work  nbc came back with a counter 65 000 per  episode and 12.5  but apparently they quickly changed  their minds because she was fired after  filming only one more episode her  character was killed off and the show  was first renamed valerie's family and  eventually the hogan family harper had  the last laugh though winning nearly two  million dollars in a wrongful  termination lawsuit in court  in july 2012 jennifer lopez told the  world she was leaving her position as  judge on american idol she broke the  news on ryan seacrest's radio show on  the air just a day after aerosmith front  man stephen tyler announced his own exit  from the show at the time j lo told  seacrest she was leaving because idol  was monopolizing her time explaining i  honestly feel like the time has come  that i have to get back to doing the  other things that i have to do according  to the rap though jayla was actually  fired for demanding too much money they  claimed jayla was asking for a raise  from 15 million dollars per season to 17  million dollars but since ratings were  declining fox instead fired her of  course between her musical career her  acting and more it's doubtful jlo felt  much financial hardship in the interim  but even if she had it wouldn't matter  much she was rehired the following year  and remained a judge until the end of  the series time on fox i missed  everything about it it was really hard  for me to walk away when i did  hard to believe but toby maguire was  actually fired from spider-man 2 over  salary demands nearly derailing the  beloved franchise as recounted by screen  crush when mcguire learned how much sony  had made from 2002's spider-man his 4  million dollar payday seemed far too  small a slice of the pie so during  negotiations maguire simply didn't show  up when he was supposed to report to get  his face and body scanned for the visual  effects of spider-man 2 maguire said  that due to mild discomfort in his lower  back from an injury sustained while  filming 2003's seabiscuit he wouldn't be  able to show up for work  rather than suffer what they saw as a  bluff on mcguire's part sony fired him  and soon afterward director sam raimi  and some of the producers met with  future spidey villain jake gyllenhaal  about taking over the role maguire  reportedly had his future father-in-law  who was then vice chairman of nbc  universal helped convince sony to bring  maguire back instead  for the first six seasons of the drama  one tree hill chad michael murray played  the series main character and narrator  lucas scott but at the end of the sixth  season lucas and his wife left tree hill  north carolina with their newborn  daughter after their departure one tree  hill stuck around for three more seasons  so why did murray leave the show turns  out he was fired over money demands  after trying to negotiate a pay raise  for the show's seventh season marie then  appealed to the fans to save his job  saying they're not bringing me back next  year because they want to save money  start blogging and being pissed off  apparently whatever blogging or other  attempts were made by fans weren't  successful because the final three  seasons of the drama unfolded without  him for the most part other than a cameo  appearance part way through the show's  final season  there remains no official word on  exactly why jaime foxworth's family  matters character disappeared in the  show's fourth season beyond co-creator  william bickley saying it was for quote  budget considerations in mama's wedding  boxworth's character judy is present  then at the start of the next episode  she's gone and is basically never  mentioned again rather than recast judy  for the show's five remaining seasons  her existence was utterly forgotten one  persistent rumor puts the blame for her  departure on the doorstep of foxworth's  mother though supposedly foxworth's  mother gwyn fox demanded more money for  her daughter instead boxworth was fired  none of that has ever been confirmed  though and it may all be rumor what's  not a rumor though is the fact that  foxworth never got a job acting on  television again  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stars are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

